  "text": "The longest any machine has lasted on Venus is just over two hours. Could a robot survive there? The ground is hot enough to melt lead. The air presses like the sea nearly a kilometer down. In 1982, a Soviet lander sent back color photos, then the heat won. The full film, What Happened to Venus?",
